# Ingest

Capture the kind, then let placement put it on a surface. Do not invent a third inbox.

## Offload (chat / manual)

Default is a list. A dated **event** (the day something happens) goes on Schedule. A dated **chore** stays on the list.

- Groceries → Shopping.
- Ordinary tasks, even with a date → **General to do** (`collection_id`). “Book the eye test on 5 December”, “email the teacher about the trip”, “return the form by the 19th”, “buy shoes for the wedding”. Never skip the to-do list because there are 2+ children.
- **Occurrence** when the date is clearly the day something happens (`statedEventFromOffload`): “X is on 23 October”, “spa day on 12 June”, “on Wednesday next week”, “for next Tuesday”. Not a closed list of event words. Bare “Friday” or “next week” alone is not enough. Code also recovers this when the model titles the work (`Book flights`) but the sentence dates the event.
- Then: parent `occurrence` + `occurs_at`, **no** `collection_id`. Named work (speech, RSVP, book flights) → **child obligations**. Showing up is not work — drop “arrive at the hospital”, “arrive by 7:30”, “attend the appointment”, and any child that restates the event title. A named happening they already have (spa, parents evening, haircut, sports day) is the event — Schedule, and Radar only while the day is still ahead. Pre-op, operation, and dentist are Schedule-only unless there is real extra work. Put the clock on `occurs_at`. Headline + sub is enough. Admin-led sentences stay on the list. High-confidence email/chat vs calendar matches merge (`_shared/cross-source.ts`); the calendar `occurrence` is canonical. Medium matches stay separate. After merge, drop children that restate that event.
- Mixed line (“out of oat milk and email Taya’s teacher”) **splits**. `isGroceryOffload` is false when the text also has email/teacher/call/book. Do not let the model title (`Oat milk`) swallow the task.

## Email / calendar

- Hold: one heads-up, `due_at` null. Drop undated “buy a new X” children (`splitParentAndChildren`).
- Stated kit: persist each line, **`due_at` null** (`isEventKitTitle`). Do not copy the event day onto goggles/towel so they look like Home deadlines.
- Form / RSVP / payment: dated obligations. Party with “reply so we know numbers” → parent **occurrence** (if the day is known) or **context_only**, child **RSVP**. Not the party as a Home to-do.
- Named dated events may be `occurrence` from email too — same bar as Offload. Nursery closed stays `context_only`.
- Confirmation of admin ("authorisation is in place", "form received") with no new action is ignored. Do not complete open work from it — the user ticks the item in the app. Same-person same-day admission/operation/surgery still merge when the mail has real work. Do not title the parent as the auth problem.
- “No presents/gifts” → drop Present, Card, and donation/charity leftovers.
- Interviews, 1:1s, standups: `obligations: []`. Never invent research / examples / JD.
- Junk titles (`New`, Untitled) are not items.

## Lists

Never `createCustomCollection` from checklist count. Shopping and General to do only, unless the user created the list on Plan.
